    "field": "Glacier inventory",
    "problem": "Previous assessments of Austrian glaciers were highly inaccurate, relying on outdated, incomplete, and non-simultaneous surveys from as early as 1870, which resulted in a significant overestimation of the total glacier area in contemporary textbooks.",
    "method": "This paper describes the creation of a new Austrian glacier inventory for 1969 based on photogrammetric evaluation of dedicated aerial photographs, with additional assessment of areal losses since 1850 and 1920 by mapping historical moraines from the same imagery.",
    "task": "The task is to create a new inventory of Austrian glaciers for 1969 using aerial photography and to evaluate the changes in glacier area and volume by comparing the results with historical data from 1850 and 1920.",
